> Outside the promise, the threshold has no promised meaning

For an arbitrary truth table P_0 depends only on its number of ones; the
remaining spectrum depends on their positions. With four bits and one one,
P_0=49/64=0.765625, and the compatibility flag says constant despite the
nonconstant table. With two bits and table [0,0,0,1], P_0=1/4, and the flag
says false despite the table being unbalanced. Native trace promise categories
identify both as neither. The classical API also relies on the promise:
querying inputs 0 through 8 misses a four-bit function's lone one at input 15.

Balanced functions need not be parities or concentrate at a single nonzero
basis state. The piecewise function below uses the low bit on x<4 and the
next bit on x≥4. Its truth table [0,1,0,1,0,0,1,1] is balanced, but its final
distribution has four nonzero probabilities of one quarter each. The sweep
then checks every possible number of ones on the four-bit domain.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dj_promise_boundary.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  const auto near=dm::algorithms::deutsch_jozsa_trace(4,[](std::size_t x){return x==15;});
  const auto and2=dm::algorithms::deutsch_jozsa_trace(2,[](std::size_t x){return x==3;});
  const auto misleading=dm::algorithms::deutsch_jozsa_classical(4,[](std::size_t x){return x==15;});
  std::print("One one among 16: P0 {:.6f}; threshold constant {}; promise neither {}.\n\n",near.result.prob_all_zero,near.result.constant,near.promise==dm::algorithms::DeutschJozsaPromise::neither);
  std::print("AND on two bits: P0 {:.6f}; threshold constant {}; promise neither {}.\n\n",and2.result.prob_all_zero,and2.result.constant,and2.promise==dm::algorithms::DeutschJozsaPromise::neither);
  std::print("Off-promise classical control: constant {}; queries {}.\n\n",misleading.constant,misleading.queries);
  const auto nonlinear=dm::algorithms::deutsch_jozsa_trace(3,[](std::size_t x){return x<4?(x&1):((x>>1)&1);});
  std::print("Nonlinear balanced table {}; promise balanced {}.\n\n",nonlinear.truth_table,nonlinear.promise==dm::algorithms::DeutschJozsaPromise::balanced);
  const auto probabilities=dm::algorithms::probabilities(nonlinear.final_state);
  std::print("| outcome y | probability |\n| ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(std::size_t y=0;y<probabilities.size();++y)std::print("| {:03b} | {:.6f} |\n",y,probabilities[y]);
  std::vector<double> fractions,p0,formula;double residual=0;
  for(std::size_t w=0;w<=16;++w) {
    const auto t=dm::algorithms::deutsch_jozsa_trace(4,[w](std::size_t x){return x<w;});
    fractions.push_back(double(w)/16);p0.push_back(t.result.prob_all_zero);formula.push_back(t.mean_phase*t.mean_phase);
    residual=std::max(residual,std::abs(p0.back()-formula.back()));
  }
  if(residual>1e-12 || near.promise!=dm::algorithms::DeutschJozsaPromise::neither || and2.promise!=dm::algorithms::DeutschJozsaPromise::neither)return 1;
  std::print("\nAll 17 four-bit one-counts checked; maximum probability residual {:.3e}.\n",residual);
  auto p=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();p.line(fractions,formula,"count formula",{37,99,235},2)
   .points(fractions,p0,"actual circuit",{234,88,12},5).abline_h(.5,{100,116,139},1)
   .title("Promise locations: endpoints constant, midpoint balanced")
   .x_label("fraction of effective ones, w/16").y_label("P(all zero) = (1 - 2w/16)^2")
   .y_limits(-.05,1.12).size(1100,570).save_svg("build/dj_promise_boundary.svg");
}
```
