> Query complexity and the cost of running this simulator

For n≥1, a deterministic classical algorithm can be forced to receive the
same answer at N/2 distinct inputs. Those observations are compatible with
a constant function and with a balanced completion, so it needs another
query in the worst case. N/2+1 queries suffice: two different outputs mean
balanced, while N/2+1 equal outputs exclude balanced. The sequential API
implements this rule. The top-bit control attains its bound exactly; low-bit
parity instead stops after two queries. For n=0 the domain contains one
input and only a constant case; both APIs call that input once.

The ideal circuit uses one logical phase query and 2n single-qubit Hadamards,
excluding oracle construction and measurement hardware. This classical
simulator instead stores N complex amplitudes, makes N callback calls and
executes 2n×N/2=nN amplitude-pair updates. Each callback's own cost is extra.
The rich trace retains three actual states and one integer table: O(N) storage;
the original API retains only its working state, also O(N). A full classical
truth-table count could check the promise with N evaluations and O(1) extra
storage, without simulating any circuit. The new trace's inspection of every
callback value is likewise classical evidence, not an extra physical promise
test obtained for free from a quantum measurement.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/dj_query_work.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
  std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
  std::vector<double> bits,logical,callbacks,classical,pairs;
  std::print("| n | basis states | logical oracle applications | actual simulator callbacks | Hadamards | actual pair updates | classical top-bit queries |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
  for(int n:{1,2,4,8,12,16}) {
    const std::function<int(std::size_t)> oracle=[n](std::size_t x){return (x>>(n-1))&1;};
    const auto t=dm::algorithms::deutsch_jozsa_trace(n,oracle);const auto c=dm::algorithms::deutsch_jozsa_classical(n,oracle);
    if(c.queries!=t.truth_table.size()/2+1 || t.work.butterflies!=std::size_t(n)*t.truth_table.size())return 1;
    std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",n,t.truth_table.size(),t.work.oracle_applications,t.work.callback_calls,t.work.hadamard_gates,t.work.butterflies,c.queries);
    bits.push_back(n);logical.push_back(std::log2(double(t.work.oracle_applications)));callbacks.push_back(std::log2(double(t.work.callback_calls)));
    classical.push_back(std::log2(double(c.queries)));pairs.push_back(std::log2(double(t.work.butterflies)));
  }
  auto query=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();query.line(bits,logical,"logical quantum",{22,163,74},2)
   .line(bits,classical,"classical top bit",{234,88,12},2).line(bits,callbacks,"simulator callbacks",{37,99,235},2)
   .title("Quantum and classical oracle counts").x_label("input bits n").y_label("log2(actual count)").y_limits(-.6,20);
  auto simulation=dm::graphics::RPlot::create();simulation.line(bits,callbacks,"callbacks",{37,99,235},2).line(bits,pairs,"pair updates",{124,58,237},2)
   .title("Exponential classical simulation work").x_label("input bits n").y_label("log2(actual primitive count)").y_limits(-.6,24);
  dm::graphics::RLayout::create(1,2).add(query).add(simulation).size(1100,520).title("One logical oracle query still costs 2^n C++ callback calls").fit_panels().save_svg("build/dj_query_work.svg");
  int rejected=0,calls=0;const std::function<int(std::size_t)> counter=[&](std::size_t){++calls;return 0;};
  try{dm::algorithms::deutsch_jozsa_trace(-1,counter,1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++rejected;}
  try{dm::algorithms::deutsch_jozsa_trace(4,counter,15);}catch(const std::length_error&){++rejected;}
  try{dm::algorithms::deutsch_jozsa_trace(4,{},1);}catch(const std::invalid_argument&){++rejected;}
  if(rejected!=3 || calls!=0)return 1;
  std::print("\nThree expected domain/cap/empty-callback rejections; callback calls before rejection {}. Exact cap 16 and zero-disabled optional cap both succeed.\n",calls);
  dm::algorithms::deutsch_jozsa_trace(4,counter,16);dm::algorithms::deutsch_jozsa_trace(4,counter,0);
  if(calls!=32)return 1;
}
```
